### ClearWood Furnitures — Catalog management phase (dynamic catalog)
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.
### Everything here is data an admin changes without a deploy; the storefront reads it back.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Sign in (sets cw_adm_at / cw_adm_rt / cw_adm_csrf)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@clearwood.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe@12345"
}

###
@csrf = {{adminLogin.response.headers.$['set-cookie'][2]}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------ settings

### 2. Catalog settings: page sizes, out-of-stock policy, new-arrival window, badge words
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/settings

### 3. Shorten the new-arrival window and reword one badge (badges merge per code; null = off)
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "newArrivalDays": 21,
  "badges": {
    "NEW_ARRIVAL": { "label": "Just in", "color": "#7E8C77" },
    "IN_HOUSE": { "label": "Made in our workshop", "color": null }
  }
}

### 4. 422: the default page size may not exceed the maximum
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "defaultPageSize": 90, "maxPageSize": 60 }

### ------------------------------------------------------------ admin product table

### 5. Compact rows, filtered server-side: publication state, merchandising, date range
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products?publication=LIVE&customizable=true&isFeatured=true&createdFrom=2026-01-01&sort=createdAt&order=desc&limit=20

# @name productPage
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products?limit=1

###
@productId = {{productPage.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 6. Schedule it: publishedAt in the future means SCHEDULED; the reconciler lists it on time
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/publish
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "publishAt": "2026-10-01T04:30:00.000Z" }

### 7. Publish now instead (no body)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/publish
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 8. Bulk merchandising: featured until a date, with the product's own badge
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/bulk
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "action": "SET_MERCHANDISING",
  "ids": ["{{productId}}"],
  "merchandising": {
    "isFeatured": true,
    "featuredUntil": "2026-10-15T18:29:00.000Z",
    "badgeText": "Festive pick",
    "badgeColor": "#B4613A"
  }
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------ category merchandising

# @name tree
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/tree

###
@sofasId = {{tree.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 9. A category's own products in the order its CURATED listing shows them
# @name curated
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{sofasId}}/products?limit=5

###
@firstLinked = {{curated.response.body.data.0.productId}}

### 10. Move one to the front (422 for a product that is not in the category)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/{{sofasId}}/products/reorder
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "items": [{ "id": "{{firstLinked}}", "position": 0 }] }

### 11. The storefront grid in curated order reflects it at once
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=sofas&sort=CURATED&limit=5

### ------------------------------------------------------------ rule categories

### 12. "New Arrivals" is a rule: live within the window (or flagged), no manual tagging
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=new-arrivals&limit=5

### 13. "Special Collection" under Sofas lists every Sofas product flagged special
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=special-collection-sofas&limit=5

### ------------------------------------------------------------ collections

# @name collections
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/collections?includeDeleted=true

###
@collectionId = {{collections.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 14. Restore a soft-deleted collection (AUTOMATIC ones are re-evaluated)
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/collections/{{collectionId}}/restore
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------ contract work

### 15. The contract-work service line: kind SERVICE, leadFormKey "contract-work"
GET {{api}}/catalog/categories/contract-based-work

### 16. A customer sends a project request from one of its pages (never an order)
POST {{api}}/enquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "formKey": "contract-work",
  "categorySlug": "custom-hotel-furniture",
  "name": "Asha Rao",
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "phone": "+91 98450 00000",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "companyName": "Lakeview Suites",
  "quantity": 40,
  "budgetPaise": 250000000,
  "message": "Headboards and lounge chairs for 40 rooms.",
  "details": { "rooms": 40, "timeline": "Q1 2027" }
}

### 17. 422: a form key that no live surface offers
POST {{api}}/enquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{ "formKey": "not-offered", "name": "Test", "email": "t@example.com" }

### 18. The admin queue (lead.enquiry.read)
# @name enquiries
GET {{api}}/admin/enquiries?status=NEW&formKey=contract-work

###
@enquiryId = {{enquiries.response.body.data.0.id}}

GET {{api}}/admin/enquiries/{{enquiryId}}

### 19. Move it along (lead.enquiry.update; assignedToId also needs lead.enquiry.assign)
PATCH {{api}}/admin/enquiries/{{enquiryId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "status": "CONTACTED", "adminNote": "Site visit booked", "version": 0 }
